SELECT
    b.mandt,
    b.bukrs,
    b.kunnr,
    b.gjahr,
    b.belnr,
    b.buzei,

    /* Payment Term */
    b.zterm,
    t.ztagg,          -- baseline / net days (config dependent)
    t.zbd1t,          -- cash discount 1 days
    t.zbd2t,          -- cash discount 2 days
    u.text1 AS payment_term_text,

    /* Dates */
    b.zfbdt AS baseline_date,
    b.faedt AS due_date,
    b.augdt AS clearing_date,

    /* Amounts */
    b.dmbtr AS amount_local,

    /* SD Billing Link */
    b.vbeln AS billing_doc,
    v.fkart AS billing_type,
    v.vkorg AS sales_org,
    v.kunrg AS payer,
    v.fkdat AS billing_date,
    v.waerk AS billing_currency

FROM bsad b

/* Payment Terms Customizing */
LEFT JOIN t052 t
  ON t.mandt = b.mandt
 AND t.zterm = b.zterm

/* Payment Term Texts */
LEFT JOIN t052u u
  ON u.mandt = b.mandt
 AND u.zterm = b.zterm
 AND u.spras = 'E'          -- English text

/* Billing Header Join */
LEFT JOIN vbrk v
  ON v.mandt = b.mandt
 AND v.vbeln = b.vbeln      -- KEY JOIN (FI → SD)

WHERE b.mandt = '100';


BSAD → VBRK
   •   BSAD.VBELN contains the originating billing document for AR items posted from SD.
   •   If your FI postings come from SD billing, this will always match VBRK.VBELN.

(If VBELN is empty → it is NOT an SD invoice.)

